    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Windom was founded in 1879 as a station on the Atchison, Topeka and Santa Fe Railway, just 13 miles west of McPherson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/windom_kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers in Windom lived in sod houses and braved 1874 grasshopper plagues, relying on mutual aid to survive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/windom_kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Windom has seen heat waves over 110°F in 1936 and cold snaps below –20°F in 1989, showcasing its climate extremes.",
